  "query_preview": "..\nSplit flow pattern continues through the weekend with open trough\nover the desert southwest and zonal flow in the north. Southwest\ntrough will lift north as another low slides south along the west\ncoast from the Gulf of Alaska. By midweek a wave will push east\nfrom the coast through the northern Rockies. \n\nThis will help maintain below average temperatures across\nnortheast Montana over the next several days. Weak shortwaves \nmoving east may produce isolated or widely scattered chances for \nprecipitation, though widespread significant precipitation \nappears unlikely.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo changes to the going NBM forecast.",
